{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794320801627,"sessionID":"ses_e3a3359fbffe97vzjLW1G2XYZe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_U8wHQCvucyMmFTGWao7q9q2g","state":{"status":"error","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/frontend/src/lib.test.ts\n+import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\n+import test from \"node:test\";\n+import { addDays, changeMonth, dateKey, daysForView, eventsOnDay, monthDays, periodTitle, timeSegments, weekStart } from \"./lib.ts\";\n+import type { CalendarEvent } from \"./lib.ts\";\n+\n+const event = (id: number, start: string, end: string): CalendarEvent => ({ id, title: `Event ${id}`, description: null, location: null, start_time: start, end_time: end, created_at: \"2026-11-01T00:00:00Z\", created_by: \"alice\" });\n+\n+test(\"month grids start on Monday and contain the entire month\", () => {\n+  const days = monthDays(new Date(\"2026-11-10T00:00:00Z\"));\n+  assert.equal(dateKey(days[0]), \"2026-10-26\");\n+  assert.equal(dateKey(days[days.length - 1]), \"2026-12-06\");\n+  assert.equal(days.length, 42);\n+  assert.equal(days[0].getUTCDay(), 1);\n+});\n+\n+test(\"month navigation clamps dates and handles leap years\", () => {\n+  assert.equal(dateKey(changeMonth(new Date(\"2026-01-31T00:00:00Z\"), 1)), \"2026-02-28\");\n+  assert.equal(dateKey(changeMonth(new Date(\"2024-01-31T00:00:00Z\"), 1)), \"2024-02-29\");\n+  assert.equal(dateKey(changeMonth(new Date(\"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\"), -1)), \"2025-12-01\");\n+});\n+\n+test(\"week and day views use UTC boundaries\", () => {\n+  const date = new Date(\"2026-11-15T23:30:00Z\");\n+  assert.equal(dateKey(weekStart(date)), \"2026-11-09\");\n+  assert.equal(daysForView(date, \"week\").length, 7);\n+  assert.equal(daysForView(date, \"day\")[0].toISOString(), \"2026-11-15T00:00:00.000Z\");\n+  assert.equal(dateKey(addDays(new Date(\"2026-12-31T00:00:00Z\"), 1)), \"2027-01-01\");\n+});\n+\n+test(\"multi-day events appear on each overlapping day but not their midnight end date\", () => {\n+  const events = [event(1, \"2026-11-10T23:00:00Z\", \"2026-11-12T00:00:00Z\")];\n+  assert.equal(eventsOnDay(events, new Date(\"2026-11-10\")).length, 1);\n+  assert.equal(eventsOnDay(events, new Date(\"2026-11-11\")).length, 1);\n+  assert.equal(eventsOnDay(events, new Date(\"2026-11-12\")).length, 0);\n+});\n+\n+test(\"overlapping events get separate timeline columns\", () => {\n+  const segments = timeSegments([\n+    event(1, \"2026-11-10T09:00:00Z\", \"2026-11-10T11:00:00Z\"),\n+    event(2, \"2026-11-10T10:00:00Z\", \"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z\"),\n+    event(3, \"2026-11-10T14:00:00Z\", \"2026-11-10T15:00:00Z\"),\n+  ], new Date(\"2026-11-10\"));\n+  assert.equal(segments[0].columns, 2);\n+  assert.equal(segments[1].columns, 2);\n+  assert.notEqual(segments[0].column, segments[1].column);\n+  assert.equal(segments[2].columns, 1);\n+  assert.equal(segments[2].start, 840);\n+});\n+\n+test(\"period titles include both years when a week crosses a year boundary\", () => {\n+  const title = periodTitle(new Date(\"2026-12-31\"), \"week\");\n+  assert.match(title, /2026/);\n+  assert.match(title, /2027/);\n+});\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/package.json\n@@\n-    \"lint\": \"eslint .\"\n+    \"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n+    \"test\": \"node --experimental-strip-types --test src/lib.test.ts\"\n*** Update File: /workspace/README.md\n@@\n Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and hashes and is installed directly. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+Install Python dependencies with `python3 -m pip install -r backend/requirements.lock` and frontend dependencies with `npm ci` in `frontend/`.\n+Run `python3 backend/app.py` from the workspace root and `npm run dev` in `frontend/`. Vite proxies `/api` to port 8000.\n+Run `npm run build` in `frontend/` to serve the production frontend directly from Flask.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- API tests: `python3 -m unittest backend.test_app -v`\n+- Python lint (requires Ruff): `python3 -m ruff check backend`\n+- Frontend tests: `npm test` in `frontend/`\n+- Frontend lint: `npm run lint` in `frontend/`\n+- Type checks: `npm run typecheck` in `frontend/`\n+- Production build: `npm run build` in `frontend/`\n+\n+## API details\n+\n+Events require `title`, `start_time`, and `end_time`. `description` and `location` are optional and are cleared to `null` when omitted in a replacement. End time must be after start time. Validation errors return HTTP 400 with `error` and an `errors` object keyed by field.\n+Date-times use ISO 8601; dates without an offset are interpreted as UTC and responses use a trailing `Z`.\n+The list endpoint filters event start times. Date-only range boundaries include the entire date; date-time boundaries are inclusive. Results are sorted by start time.\n+Passwords are hashed; opaque bearer tokens are stored as hashes in SQLite and remain valid for 30 days across restarts. `/api/auth/me` returns the current username, and `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the current token.\n+Data is stored in `data/calendar.sqlite3`. The `DATABASE_PATH` environment variable can override the database path.\n+\n+## Docker\n+\n+Build with `docker build -t gather .` and start with `docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$PWD/data:/app/data\" gather` to persist accounts and events across container restarts.\n*** Add File: /tmp/opencode/package.json\n+{\"private\":true,\"type\":\"module\"}\n*** End Patch"},"error":"The user has specified a rule which prevents you from using this specific tool call. Here are some of the relevant rules [{\"permission\":\"*\",\"action\":\"allow\",\"pattern\":\"*\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"*\",\"action\":\"ask\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/run/home/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\"